  "live_records": {
    "q-184491": {
      "dom_id": "step-q184491",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=(-2,0)\\times {2,3}$ in the Cartesian plane?",
      "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=(-2,0)\\times {2,3}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $(-2,0)$ and whose $y$-coordinate is either $2$ or $3.$\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in (-2,0),\\,y\\in {2,3}}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $(-2,0)$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $2$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}={(x,2)\\,:\\,x\\in (-2,0)}\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14124149/assets/3ff59491671c85c444afefb827c5b7cc30d617547e88f8c87b0b7edb07c5ce90.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $(-2,0)$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $3$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}={(x,3)\\,:\\,x\\in (-2,0)}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14124149/assets/45f703cae4149be4cc973c0537a7bb4c5fcd06b5bf3e1989004d762839154112.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\nS={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $S$ can be represented by the two line segments shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14124149/assets/b501bc9b634b38c5b0f77fc7cd4e846208076014a83029428786e36488839999.png)",
