    "q-174338": {
      "dom_id": "step-q174338",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times [0,2i].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0,0.5]\\times [0,1]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,0.5],b\\in [0,1]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(0.5,0),$ $(0.5,1),$ and $(0,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14124149/assets/5a50d17270e3856778a32461449d1e1abe36376be549e460a8fcee9ef6ea194b.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times [0,2i]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,i],b\\in [0,2i]}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(i,0),$ $(i,2i),$ and $(0,2i).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14124149/assets/290a50d82323a459fbd0a790e28ff8889323cd5f08a0915f85b85a0aa0999490.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the point $(0,0):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14124149/assets/efb6d92ea0dc70fa0cbd9d82ea838b41a4eaab6ee2fc32c6fada9258a4154680.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-174338-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$∅,$ the empty set",
